{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And Midianite men, merchants, passed by and drew him up.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat), those who passed by drew him up and sold him — not the brothers. According to this, what Yosef said to them, ״אני יוסף אחיכם אשר מכרתם אותי מצרימה״ — 'I am Yosef your brother whom you sold into Egypt' — the matter is that they cast him into the pit, which was the cause of the sale. And this is what it says מצרימה, meaning that he passed from master to master and was sold many times until he was brought down to Egypt. And the sin found upon them that is explicitly enumerated among the Ten Martyrs of the Kingdom is this: that they were the cause of the sale. And great ones of the world such as they are worthy of punishment for casting their esteemed brother into a pit, and it is reckoned to them as bloodshed as though they had killed him with their own hands, in the manner of what is written (II Samuel 12:9): ״ואותו הרגת בחרב בני עמון״. For there is no difference between one who kills his fellow with his own hands or one who brings about his death, except a great judgment and a small judgment." "<b>For twenty pieces of silver.</b> We were commanded in the Torah regarding the redemption of the son that it be five sela'im, as it is written (Numbers 18:15–16): ״ופדויו מבן חדש תפדה בערכך כסף חמשת שקלים״. And the sela is four dinars; if so, five sela'im times four are twenty of silver. And this is why Onkelos translated בעשרים כסף, and did not translate בעשרין סלעין דכסף. From this you learn the commandment of redemption of the son, which is five sela'im, which are twenty of silver, because it comes to atone for the sale of Yosef, the firstborn of Rachel, who gave him the birthright, who was sold for twenty of silver."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:25.879794078Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}